course: dictionary
lesson: 16184
title: Short forms: yr
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: «Yr» is a short way to write year. Writers use it to save space in tables, charts and school notices. «Yr 4» means Year 4, a class at school. When you read it aloud, say "year".
explain: To check, swap in the full word. «A 5 yr old» becomes «a 5 year old», which still makes sense, so yr means year. The plural is yrs, as in «children 6 yrs and over», which is read aloud as "years".
explain: In quick messages, yr can also be a short way to write your or you're. «Is this yr pencil case?» means "your". Look at the words around it to see which meaning fits. Do not use this short form in school writing.
fact: Yr is an abbreviation, which means a short form of a longer word.
fact: «Yr» means year, and «yrs» means years.
fact: «Yr 4» means Year 4, a class at school in the UK, Australia and New Zealand.
fact: On a medicine box, «children 6 yrs and over» means children aged six years and older.
fact: In informal texts, «yr» can be a short way to write your or you're.
exercise: Our Yr 5 class is going on a trip. What does Yr mean here? | *Year | Yard | Yacht | Yes
exercise: The medicine box says «children 6 yrs and over». How do you read yrs aloud? | *Years | Yoghurts | Yards | Yes
exercise: In a quick text, «Is this yr pencil case?» What does yr most likely mean? | *Your | Year | Yellow | A type of cake
test: What does Yr mean in «Yr 3 swimming is on Monday»? | Yard | Yes | Young | *Year
test: Which word could replace yrs in «a boy of 8 yrs old»? | *Years | Yes | Yards | Yachts
exam: In the sentence «My yr 6 friend is 11 yrs old», what does yr mean? | Yacht | Your | *Year | Yesterday
